{"name":"Loch Blue","hex":"#609795","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"loch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lake.","A bay or arm of the sea."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of lohoch (“medicine taken by licking”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loch"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loch","blocks":[{"text":"Loch is a word meaning \"lake\" or \"sea inlet\" in Scottish and Irish Gaelic, subsequently borrowed into English. In Irish contexts, it often appears in the anglicized form \"lough\". A small loch is sometimes called a lochan. Lochs which connect to the sea may be called \"sea lochs\" or \"sea loughs\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Ben_Lomond_Scotland.jpg/330px-Ben_Lomond_Scotland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loch","wikidata":"Q1172903"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg/330px-LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg/330px-LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Looking down Loch Long, a long sea loch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALochLong(StevePartridge)Nov2007.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Loch_Lubnaig_%28223068248%29.jpg/500px-Loch_Lubnaig_%28223068248%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Loch_Lubnaig_%28223068248%29.jpg/1280px-Loch_Lubnaig_%28223068248%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Loch_Lubnaig_%28223068248%29.jpg/500px-Loch_Lubnaig_%28223068248%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Loch Lubnaig, a reservoir","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoch_Lubnaig_(223068248).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Lake_of_Menteith_looking_towards_Port_of_Monteith.jpg/500px-Lake_of_Menteith_looking_towards_Port_of_Monteith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Lake_of_Menteith_looking_towards_Port_of_M